      "gridPos": {"h": 8, "w": 24, "x": 0, "y": 23},
      "id": 22,
      "description": "Bytes handed back to cache callers vs bytes pulled from origin (#1513). This replaces a served/received pair built on decdn_bytes_{served,received}_total, neither of which the exporter has ever emitted. The cache counters are the closest true equivalent and carry a reading the originals did not: their ratio is the origin-egress amplification factor — 1.0 while the node is a pure pass-through, trending to 0 as content gets re-served from cache.",
      "options": {"legend": {"displayMode": "table", "placement": "right", "showLegend": true}, "tooltip": {"mode": "multi"}},
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {"type": "prometheus", "uid": "${DS_PROMETHEUS}"},
          "expr": "rate(decdn_cache_bytes_returned_total{instance=~\"$instance\"}[5m])",
          "legendFormat": "served — {{instance}}",
          "refId": "A"
        },
        {
          "datasource": {"type": "prometheus", "uid": "${DS_PROMETHEUS}"},
          "expr": "rate(decdn_cache_pull_through_bytes_total{instance=~\"$instance\"}[5m])",
          "legendFormat": "origin pull-through — {{instance}}",
          "refId": "B"
        }
      ],
      "title": "Throughput (served vs origin pull-through)",
      "type": "timeseries"
    },
    {
      "datasource": {"type": "prometheus", "uid": "${DS_PROMETHEUS}"},
      "description": "Delivery refusals that share the NotFound wire code (#1520). The first three are payment-class; `cache miss` is availability and is plotted as the baseline to read the others against. All four collapse to the same NotFound wire code so a client cannot tell them apart — these counters are the only place the cause exists. `insufficient deposit` is fed by three guards (the pre-spend miss floor, the window tier's ceiling, and the direct-serve ceiling) and cannot attribute a spike to one; the node's throttled warn! line does. Sustained insufficient-deposit means either clients running dry (no action) or this node's chain watcher lagging an on-chain top-up, in which case funded clients are being turned away.",
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "color": {"mode": "palette-classic"},
          "custom": {"drawStyle": "bars", "fillOpacity": 60, "lineWidth": 1, "stacking": {"mode": "normal"}},
          "unit": "ops"
        }
      },
      "gridPos": {"h": 8, "w": 24, "x": 0, "y": 31},
      "id": 23,
      "options": {"legend": {"displayMode": "table", "placement": "right", "showLegend": true}, "tooltip": {"mode": "multi"}},
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {"type": "prometheus", "uid": "${DS_PROMETHEUS}"},
          "expr": "sum by (instance) (rate(decdn_serve_stream_rejected_insufficient_deposit_total{instance=~\"$instance\"}[5m]))",
          "legendFormat": "insufficient deposit",
          "refId": "A"
        },
        {
          "datasource": {"type": "prometheus", "uid": "${DS_PROMETHEUS}"},
          "expr": "sum by (instance) (rate(decdn_serve_stream_rejected_unknown_channel_total{instance=~\"$instance\"}[5m]))",
          "legendFormat": "unknown channel",
          "refId": "B"
        },
        {
          "datasource": {"type": "prometheus", "uid": "${DS_PROMETHEUS}"},
          "expr": "sum by (instance) (rate(decdn_serve_stream_rejected_owner_mismatch_total{instance=~\"$instance\"}[5m]))",
          "legendFormat": "owner mismatch",
          "refId": "C"
        },
        {
          "datasource": {"type": "prometheus", "uid": "${DS_PROMETHEUS}"},
          "expr": "sum by (instance) (rate(decdn_serve_stream_rejected_cache_miss_total{instance=~\"$instance\"}[5m]))",
          "legendFormat": "cache miss",
          "refId": "D"
        },
        {
          "datasource": {"type": "prometheus", "uid": "${DS_PROMETHEUS}"},
          "expr": "sum by (instance) (rate(decdn_serve_stream_rejected_internal_error_total{instance=~\"$instance\"}[5m]))",
          "legendFormat": "internal error",
          "refId": "E"
        }
      ],
      "title": "Payment-class serve refusals (all collapse to NotFound)",
      "type": "timeseries"
    },
